 outcomes have absolute value 3000, so both have the same minimum absolute value. Thus, the sure outcome is not uniquely defined. Therefore, the reason cannot be applied to distinguish between A and B in a clear way. So, the decision reason is not applicable to this problem due to ambiguity in identifying a sure outcome.",
